# Reactive Surface Water Material RT Report - 2026-07-06

## Scope

- Replaces the experimental Water visual path with Material/RenderTarget ping-pong for the public normal-map RT.
- Keeps existing Niagara assets intact; this pass proves an alternate water route only.
- Height step implements the user-provided no-rain HTML formula.
- Height ping-pong RTs use `RTF_RGBA32F`; public normal output remains `RTF_RGBA16F`.
- Source position is snapped to the RT cell grid before impulse evaluation to match the HTML `Math.round()` coordinate behavior.
- Water window default is `1500.0cm` (15m x 15m), with source-centered fallback when no explicit window origin is supplied.
- Water damping default is `0.9813`: the previous `0.945` decay time is stretched about 3x without exceeding the solver clamp.
- Trail taps are parameterized: length `360.0cm`, strength `0.65`, fade `0.82`, tap count `6.0`.

## Assets

- Step material: `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Water/M_RS_WaterRT_Step`
- Normal material: `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Water/M_RS_WaterRT_Normal`
- Height RT A/B: `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Water/RT_RS_Water_HeightA`, `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Water/RT_RS_Water_HeightB`
- Public normal RT: `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Water/RT_RS_Water`

